  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_3fe458a035c14c22aca1e874e111cdd3",
      "statement": "ENS exposes three Treasury-facing APIs: POST /ens/v3/notifications (EP-ENS-01) to send a registered event with an approved template, POST /ens/v3/subscriptions (EP-ENS-02) to create a per-user subscription filtered by eventType and accountId, and GET /ens/v3/event-types?domain=TRS (EP-ENS-03) to read the TRS event catalog.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/ens-int-3.2-enterprise-notification-service-integration-guide.md#L77-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:602c087a2c9e2432ac2347e20e31b61f7ea58215954e49e021f04cf41bb8681e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25c2306c56404e30a5ddbd4e7bace154",
      "statement": "The current Treasury (TRS) event catalog has exactly six live event types: TRS.WIRE.APPROVAL_REQUIRED, TRS.WIRE.RELEASED, TRS.WIRE.REJECTED, TRS.WIRE.INCOMING_POSTED, TRS.ACH.STATUS_CHANGED, and TRS.ACH.RETURN_RECEIVED, each with a fixed producer, trigger, and template.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/ens-int-3.2-enterprise-notification-service-integration-guide.md#L53-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6e04e2498a7a101676059970f116757f6e72b398c75e422a9cef0b7d123a4b5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_97b659da1c944c32b453f99f160a79f3",
      "statement": "No ENS event types are registered for wire network acceptance, beneficiary credit confirmation (gpi ACCC), wire returns, gpi milestones, or client action required on held wires; this is an explicit, named gap in the TRS catalog.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/ens-int-3.2-enterprise-notification-service-integration-guide.md#L75-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c711a202e3c02b999cc47706e6568e6e339edc12411a572c9c0f6bdb3ece5e3c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f0952318bb94faa8dc9ca313b4ced06",
      "statement": "ENS subscriptions can only be scoped to an event type plus optional accountId/amount filters; subscribing to an individual entity (e.g., a specific paymentId) is unsupported until the planned ENS-1120 entity-level subscription work (targeted 2027-H1), so producers needing a specific recipient today use a producer-resolved-recipients send pattern instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/ens-int-3.2-enterprise-notification-service-integration-guide.md#L49-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b6750fc41945eae6836d5115964229ec2e5835b12941bb5e45adddb0e807434:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9a9613784a24f7fa548fc5848a685f0",
      "statement": "Onboarding a new ENS event type is a defined five-step process (ServiceNow catalog item, payload/recipient-resolution design, DRC template review, ENS configuration/testing, producer UAT) with a published 6-week SLA to production, and requests submitted after 2026-11-20 are deferred past the year-end change freeze.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/ens-int-3.2-enterprise-notification-service-integration-guide.md#L35-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba50d9789bac47aeb78c8b0be58c5016a66c7b51eeb9632461c33cf56926fe22:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ea80c8b73244ae89dd8b98aef129dc0",
      "statement": "Wire Center (cbo-wire-bff) currently produces only three of the six live TRS event types (TRS.WIRE.APPROVAL_REQUIRED, TRS.WIRE.RELEASED, TRS.WIRE.REJECTED), each triggered directly off a PPH v1 status value, via a synchronous call to POST /ens/v3/notifications (EP-ENS-01); TRS.WIRE.INCOMING_POSTED is produced by CDP and the TRS.ACH.* events are produced by CBO SPS, not Wire Center.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/cbo-arch-wc-4.1-wire-center-current-state-architecture.md#L107-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94cc22eab336aa0ae3d0741801269d37e1ff13ccd00cd112fc9aab6ee6139fdc:"
        },
